' ==============================================================================
' @file 4-3-crisismap-domain-model.puml
' @brief Structural class diagram defining the domain model and application services.
'
' @details
' This artifact models the core business logic, entity structures, and application 
' services for the Crisis Map disaster reporting flow. It enforces strict 
' architectural boundaries by categorizing classes into structural abstraction 
' levels (Application Layer vs. Domain Layer).
'
' Architectural Scope & Rationale:
' This model is explicitly scoped to the structural design and domain tier. 
' It utilizes Domain-Driven Design (DDD) concepts by distinguishing between 
' Aggregate Roots (DisasterReport), Value Objects (Location), and Application 
' Services (ReportWorkflow). The persistence mechanism is abstracted via the 
' ReportRepository interface to maintain domain purity.
'
' System Requirements Addressed:
' This model dictates the software implementation by defining:
' - The encapsulation of domain state and controlled state transitions.
' - The separation of Application workflows from Domain logic.
' - The exact multiplicities and lifecycle dependencies between classes.
'
' Author(s): Vlado Sruk
' Context: Software Engineering Course
'
' AI Usage Disclosure:
' Designed by Vlado Sruk. AI-assisted revision and documentation comments were
' reviewed by the author, who is responsible for the final content.
'
' Traceability Note:
' The structural properties, methods, and relationships defined herein must 
' strictly map to the finalized object-oriented source code. Any deviations 
' introduced during development must be retroactively updated in this model 
' to maintain evidence chain completeness.
'
' Diagram level: Structural / Domain Design
' Diagram type:  Class Diagram
' ==============================================================================
@startuml

title 

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' ==============================================================================
' Application Layer 
' Orchestrates use cases and delegates to the domain.
' ==============================================================================
package "Application Layer" {
  
  class ReportWorkflow <<Service>> {
    +submit(location: Location, severity: Severity): DisasterReport
    +approve(reportId: UUID): void
    +reject(reportId: UUID, reason: String): void
    +close(reportId: UUID): void
  }
  
}

' ==============================================================================
' Domain Layer 
' Encapsulates core business state, rules, and logic.
' ==============================================================================
package "Domain Layer" {

  class DisasterReport <<Entity>> <<AggregateRoot>> {
    -id: UUID
    -status: ReportStatus
    -severity: Severity
    +approve(): void
    +reject(reason: String): void
    +close(): void
  }
  
  class Location <<ValueObject>> {
    +latitude: Decimal
    +longitude: Decimal
  }
  
  enum ReportStatus <<Enum>> {
    SUBMITTED
    VISIBLE
    REJECTED
    CLOSED
  }
  
  enum Severity <<Enum>> {
    LOW
    MEDIUM
    HIGH
  }
  
  interface ReportRepository <<Repository>> {
    +findById(id: UUID): DisasterReport
    +save(report: DisasterReport): void
  }
  
}

' ==============================================================================
' Structural Relationships & Multiplicities
' ==============================================================================

' Composition mapping (Value Object lifecycle is bound to the Entity)
DisasterReport "1" *-- "1" Location : has ►

' Application Service dependencies on the Domain
ReportWorkflow "1" --> "0..*" DisasterReport : creates / changes ►
ReportWorkflow "1" --> "1" ReportRepository : loads / saves ►

' ==============================================================================
'  Constraints
' ==============================================================================

note right of DisasterReport
  Valid state transitions:
  - approve() : SUBMITTED -> VISIBLE
  - reject()  : SUBMITTED -> REJECTED
  - close()   : VISIBLE   -> CLOSED

  Status must only be changed using these 
  methods to protect data integrity.

end note


@enduml